# Whitelist repo: version ONLY the rulebook (CLAUDE.md, harness, memory, skills).
# Everything else in ~/.claude (settings, sessions, caches, tokens) stays untracked.
# skills/ added 2026-08-26: the skill caches ARE rulebook — harness lessons are
# compiled INTO them, so edits there were landing untracked and unrecoverable.
*
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
# Root README (added 2026-09-06). The whitelist's `*` had silently excluded it,
# which is why the repo had no landing page on GitHub for two months. Any NEW
# root-level file needs its own negation here or it is invisible to `git add`
# with no error.
!README.md
!harness/
!harness/**
!memory/
!memory/**
!skills/
!skills/**

# Manual pre-edit side-car snapshots (*.bak-<tag>) land INSIDE the whitelisted
# dirs above, so `*` never catches them and a wholesale `git add memory/` would
# commit them. Last matching rule wins, so this must stay below the negations.
# Added 2026-08-27 after two appeared during a memory/ edit; widened same day
# from the literal *.bak-nullso to the whole family.
*.bak-*
*.bak
!lib/
!lib/grok_preflight.py
# Added 2026-09-06. Both are cited by tracked memory files, which pointed at
# paths the repo did not ship. Neither holds a secret: keypool reads env vars
# only (secrets stay in ~/.zshenv), and debt-scan never prints a matched value
# — its --self-test asserts no 6+ char run of a planted secret reaches output.
# groqcall.py stays out (Groq is a suspended route) as does nimroute.py.
!lib/keypool.py
!lib/debt-scan.mjs

# Hooks: sources + tests only. hooks.log is a runtime log, *.bak* are snapshots,
# settings.json is machine-specific (absolute paths, permissions, MCP) — ship the
# example instead.
!hooks/
!hooks/*.sh
!hooks/*.py
!hooks/README.md
# hooks/harness/: the merged compaction-hook-harness repo (v22-v28 candidates,
# contract/mutant harness, review packets). Its own nested .gitignore still
# excludes run scratch (mrepwd_*/, *_cwd/, out/).
!hooks/harness/
!hooks/harness/**
!compact-context-monitor.sh
!settings.example.json
